{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "```python\ndef median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    15.0\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_list = sorted(l)\n    n = len(sorted_list)\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        # For an odd length list, the median is the middle element.\n        return float(sorted_list[n // 2])\n    else:\n        # For an even length list, the median is the average of the two middle elements.\n        mid1 = sorted_list[n // 2 - 1]\n        mid2 = sorted_list[n // 2]\n        return (float(mid1) + float(mid2)) / 2.0\n```"}
